# Git and GitHub

- Commit, push or pull only when asked. Never commit secrets.
- Short imperative commit subject, under about 50 characters.
- GitHub work goes through the `gh` CLI. If the repo has `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`, follow it.
- PRs and issues never mention Claude Code and have no "Test plan" section.
- If the repo has `.cursor/changelog-hook.json`, add the change to its changelog before opening a PR. If the config has a `"fragments"` key, add a new `<fragments dir>/<issue>-<slug>.md` file instead of editing the changelog.
